    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Prioritize early-intervention outreach by prior education, not just overall risk score.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " Students with no formal qualifications (43% withdrawal) and lower-than-A-level (35%) together represent over 12,000 students, a large, identifiable population, not a fringe case. Advising resources aimed broadly at \"at-risk students\" would be better targeted at this specific, sizable group."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Weight socioeconomic deprivation (IMD) at least as heavily as academic risk signals.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " The 0–30% IMD bands (most deprived, ~9,270 students combined) show withdrawal 6–11 points above the least-deprived bands, in a clean gradient, this is as strong a predictor as prior education, and financial/access-based support (not just academic tutoring) is the more direct intervention."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Don't allocate support budget by region.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " Withdrawal is flat across all 11 UK regions (23%–35%, no clear pattern), geography isn't where this outcome gap lives. A regional support program would likely underperform a program targeted by education level or IMD band instead."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Investigate the \"Unknown\" IMD population (971 students) before excluding them from equity-based support.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " Their unusually low withdrawal rate (21%) could reflect a genuinely different population (e.g., international/distance students) — worth confirming before assuming they don't need the same interventions as mapped UK students."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
